01:17:24.810 --> 01:17:26.230
You want to identify this, Mr. Colby?

01:17:27.440 --> 01:17:28.520
Yes, that's the envelope.

01:17:30.000 --> 01:17:31.960
Assume the $10,000 is the same.

01:17:35.610 --> 01:17:36.730
Get me a stenographer in here.

01:17:37.220 --> 01:17:38.040
He's right here, Lieutenant.

01:17:38.650 --> 01:17:38.830
Fine.

01:17:42.440 --> 01:17:43.620
Got anything to say yet, Regan?

01:17:44.950 --> 01:17:46.590
I'm speechless with your efficiency.

01:17:54.360 --> 01:17:55.200
Let's have it, Mr. Colby.

01:17:55.380 --> 01:17:59.500
You understand that this is very difficult for me.

01:18:00.640 --> 01:18:03.140
Miss Faraday has been my secretary for over six years.

01:18:03.420 --> 01:18:06.250
Her father was one of my dearest friends.

01:18:07.120 --> 01:18:07.620
I understand.

01:18:08.780 --> 01:18:13.650
Well, I was up in my room doing some work about an hour ago,

01:18:13.710 --> 01:18:15.930
and I heard a shot.

01:18:17.560 --> 01:18:19.180
First, I thought it was my imagination.

01:18:20.800 --> 01:18:22.300
Then I decided to investigate.

01:18:23.780 --> 01:18:29.220
I found Charles dead on the floor with Regan's gun beside him.

01:18:30.700 --> 01:18:35.790
the safe was open. D'Amico, that was his gun! You can't keep quiet. We'll do this without you. I gave

01:18:35.790 --> 01:18:45.990
it back to him two days ago. Who saw you? Miss Faraday. Go ahead, Mr. Colby. Well, I realized

01:18:45.990 --> 01:18:50.870
that Miss Faraday was the only person besides Charles and myself who knew the combination to

01:18:50.870 --> 01:18:55.940
the safe. Andrew, you had me open the safe yourself. A couple of nights ago, I happened

01:18:55.940 --> 01:18:59.720
to overhear a conversation between Mr. Regan and Miss Faraday.

01:19:00.000 --> 01:19:02.680
which Mexico City was mentioned.

01:19:03.410 --> 01:19:06.040
So when I called the police, I told them that.

01:19:07.250 --> 01:19:07.810
Okay, thanks.

01:19:08.140 --> 01:19:10.600
She was buying two tickets to Mexico City when we picked them up.

01:19:10.680 --> 01:19:11.600
You already told me that.

01:19:12.540 --> 01:19:13.580
What are you looking for, a promotion?

01:19:14.560 --> 01:19:15.920
Lieutenant, he knows why I had the money.

01:19:16.060 --> 01:19:16.920
He sent me for the tickets.

01:19:17.080 --> 01:19:18.940
You'll get your chance to talk later, Miss Faraday.

01:19:19.120 --> 01:19:24.440
What are you trying to do, Andrew?

01:19:26.070 --> 01:19:28.070
Everyone that's ever meant anything to you.

01:19:29.430 --> 01:19:29.790
Kroner?

01:19:30.860 --> 01:19:33.300
Charles, and now me.

01:19:34.140 --> 01:19:35.980
Lieutenant, this is very awkward for me.

01:19:36.040 --> 01:19:37.250
We're nearly finished, Miss Corby.

01:19:37.410 --> 01:19:38.590
Why do you believe him, D'Amico?

01:19:38.750 --> 01:19:39.690
Only yesterday...

01:19:39.690 --> 01:19:40.030
That was yesterday.

01:19:41.010 --> 01:19:42.650
I'm not interested in that case anymore.

01:19:42.750 --> 01:19:45.150
Personally, I got one right here that suits me fine.

01:19:45.390 --> 01:19:47.680
Look, what do you want, the truth or a quick arrest?

01:19:47.760 --> 01:19:48.500
What's your story?

01:19:49.000 --> 01:19:49.720
This is a frame.

01:19:50.680 --> 01:19:52.820
You get framed more than any guy I ever met.

01:19:53.480 --> 01:19:54.640
You're supposed to be a lawyer.

01:19:54.760 --> 01:19:55.560
Take a look at the evidence.

01:19:56.020 --> 01:19:59.590
Oh, D'Amico, you better change your charge.

01:20:00.000 --> 01:20:05.720
the corpse is still alive. Alive? We won't have him forever, but I may be able to string him along

01:20:05.720 --> 01:20:12.630
through the night. Any chance of him coming too? If we don't love him. Let me know the minute he

01:20:12.630 --> 01:20:18.070
comes around. Is it all right if we leave him here, Mr. Colby? Of course. Charles is my very

01:20:18.070 --> 01:20:21.860
dear friend. I'll see about having him moved upstairs. Don't let him near that room. Are you

01:20:21.860 --> 01:20:26.800
still running this case? I'm telling you, D'Amico, don't let this guy near him. Just a minute, Regan.

01:20:27.580 --> 01:20:29.960
You're under arrest. You're not giving any advice around here. Just...

01:20:30.000 --> 01:20:33.760
that's where your head's been one of my closest friends for years naturally i'd want to see him

01:20:33.760 --> 01:20:38.430
before he doctor says he can't be moved with him liable to pop off any minute i better wait

01:20:38.430 --> 01:20:42.420
around have a talk with him maybe we all better wait around

01:21:19.160 --> 01:21:21.150
suspects, blood on the floor.

01:21:30.000 --> 01:21:30.200
Thank you.

01:22:08.790 --> 01:22:13.400
Regan, why couldn't we tell them about Bruno?

01:22:15.240 --> 01:22:16.980
How do you think that would sound from the witness stand?

01:22:18.520 --> 01:22:20.540
I was trying to find a man named Victor Bruno

01:22:20.540 --> 01:22:24.040
because I was convinced that the other killing I'd done was murder.

01:22:27.590 --> 01:22:28.290
We figured on that one.

01:22:30.510 --> 01:22:31.870
If only somebody could find him.

01:22:32.600 --> 01:22:33.800
Bruno is probably dead, too.

01:22:34.750 --> 01:22:37.010
Otherwise, how could Colby be sure it wasn't Bruno on the phone?

01:22:38.080 --> 01:22:38.860
I suppose so.

01:22:41.050 --> 01:22:42.390
How could I be such a dope?

01:22:42.980 --> 01:22:43.200
You?

01:22:45.580 --> 01:22:47.160
I've been second-guessing the whole way.

01:22:48.650 --> 01:22:49.950
Regan, the boy detective.

01:22:52.550 --> 01:22:53.570
It's your life in worse hands.

01:22:56.550 --> 01:22:57.190
Come on in, Regan.

01:22:57.290 --> 01:22:58.790
I want to ask you a couple of questions.

01:23:00.960 --> 01:23:02.020
What about Tarrost?

01:23:02.380 --> 01:23:03.060
He's still out.

01:25:00.000 --> 01:25:23.450
since you shot him knocked him down pick him up tough break mr colby i really solved this one

01:25:23.450 --> 01:25:29.350
from left field i've had regan tail for the last three days i knew he wasn't here tonight

01:25:30.030 --> 01:25:34.230
Quite a comfort to us taxpayers to find our police department in such competent hands.

01:25:34.660 --> 01:25:35.080
Thanks.

01:25:35.240 --> 01:25:35.900
Thanks so much.

01:25:36.980 --> 01:25:39.780
Oh, uh, personally, just to keep the record straight,

01:25:40.420 --> 01:25:42.180
whatever happened to Kroner's million bucks?

01:25:43.310 --> 01:25:43.670
Funny.

01:25:44.640 --> 01:25:46.240
That's what Kroner wanted to know.

01:25:47.350 --> 01:25:49.500
Yes, very funny.

01:25:50.920 --> 01:25:51.620
Wait a minute.

01:25:52.200 --> 01:25:53.160
What do you think you're doing?

01:25:53.710 --> 01:25:57.350
He still owes my client $68.72.

01:25:58.500 --> 01:25:59.380
Well, you're a lawyer.

01:26:00.250 --> 01:26:00.690
Sue him.

01:26:10.930 --> 01:26:13.350
That D'Amico is really the answer to a maiden's prayer.

01:26:13.670 --> 01:26:14.130
You're right.

01:26:14.400 --> 01:26:15.500
He's a smart cookie.

01:26:16.260 --> 01:26:16.380
Huh?

01:26:16.540 --> 01:26:18.160
He doesn't catch everything.

01:26:18.980 --> 01:26:19.420
What's that?

01:26:20.400 --> 01:26:22.000
Tickets to Mexico City.

01:26:22.240 --> 01:26:24.060
Think we can use them?

01:26:26.420 --> 01:26:27.240
Well, forget you two.

01:26:27.300 --> 01:26:29.820
You'll have to check with my department if you're figuring out leaving the country.

01:26:30.410 --> 01:26:30.550
We'll see you next time.
